# Skills System

You have access to 512+ specialized skills organized in 7 collections. **Don't load skills by default** — only load what's needed for the current task.

## Quick Reference

| Collection | Count | Focus |
|------------|-------|-------|
| ECC | 131 | Developer workflows, security, architecture |
| Emil | 15 | UI/UX, animation, design engineering |
| Superpowers | 15 | Planning, TDD, code review, debugging |
| Marketing | 52 | CRO, SEO, copywriting, analytics, ads |
| Vercel | 8 | React, Next.js, deployment, performance |
| Claude SEO | 29 | Technical SEO, AI search, schema, local SEO |
| Agency | 262 | Full agency team: engineering, design, sales, GIS, healthcare |

## How to Use Skills

1. **Browse**: Visit the Skills Browser at https://skills-browser-odheur-gmailcoms-projects.vercel.app
2. **Search**: Use `/skill-search <query>` to find relevant skills
3. **Load**: Read the specific skill file when needed

## Skill Locations

```
.agents/skills/       → Emil's design/animation skills
.cursor/skills/       → ECC developer skills  
.superpowers/skills/  → Superpowers workflow skills
.marketing/skills/    → Marketing skills
.vercel-skills/skills/→ Vercel React/Next.js skills
.claude-seo/skills/   → Claude SEO skills
.agency/skills/       → Agency agent personalities
```

## Loading a Skill

When a task matches a skill domain, read the SKILL.md file:

```
# Example: Need CRO help
Read: .marketing/skills/cro/SKILL.md

# Example: Need animation help  
Read: .agents/skills/animate/SKILL.md

# Example: Need code review
Read: .superpowers/skills/requesting-code-review/SKILL.md
```

## Token-Efficient Workflow

1. Start with NO skills loaded
2. Identify task domain (frontend? SEO? marketing?)
3. Load 1-3 relevant skills max
4. Complete task
5. Don't carry skills to next task unless related
